              "step_num": "01",
              "step_label": "WHAT IT MEANS",
              "eyebrow": "UNLOCKED vs. CARRIER-LOCKED",
              "headline_html": "<em>Unlocked</em> works on any carrier",
              "body_html": "An unlocked phone can be activated on any network. A carrier-locked phone is tied to one carrier (AT&T, Verizon, T-Mobile) and <strong>worth less on resale</strong> because the buyer pool is smaller."
            }
          },
          {
            "template": "carousel",
            "fields": {
              "step_num": "02",
              "step_label": "WHY IT CHANGES YOUR OFFER",
              "eyebrow": "UNLOCKED vs. CARRIER-LOCKED",
              "headline_html": "<em>Unlocked phones</em> pay more",
              "body_html": "Unlocked devices have global demand. Locked phones can only be sold to users on that one carrier, so <strong>buyback offers drop 10-20%</strong>. It's not a penalty, it's market reality."
            }
          },
          {
            "template": "carousel",
            "fields": {
              "step_num": "03",
              "step_label": "HOW TO CHECK",
              "eyebrow": "UNLOCKED vs. CARRIER-LOCKED",
              "headline_html": "Check in <em>60 seconds</em>",
              "body_html": "iPhone: Settings > General > About > Carrier Lock. If it says <strong>No SIM restrictions</strong>, you're unlocked. Android: Settings > Connections > Networks > Network unlock. Or call your carrier and ask."
            }
          },
          {
            "template": "carousel",
            "fields": {
              "step_num": "04",
